8,"Sirionó Language (SRQ) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/srq/,Sirionó is an endangered indigenous language of Bolivia. It belongs to the Tupian language family. The language is used as a first language by adults only. It is taught as a subject of instruction in some schools.,Sirionó,Tupian
